\chapter*{Conventions}
\addcontentsline{toc}{chapter}{Conventions}
The metric and Fourier conventions are those of Part I,
\[
\eta_{\mu\nu}=\operatorname{diag}(+1,-1,-1,-1),\qquad
\ee^{-\ii k\cdot x}=\ee^{-\ii k^0t+\ii\mathbf k\cdot\mathbf x}.
\]
For electromagnetism we use Heaviside--Lorentz units and
\[
A^\mu=(A^0,\Afield),\qquad
F^{\mu\nu}=\partial^\mu A^\nu-\partial^\nu A^\mu,
\]
with
\[
E^i=F^{i0},\qquad F^{ij}=-\epsilon^{ijk}B^k,
\qquad \epsilon^{0123}=+1.
\]
Consequently
\[
\Efield=-\dot{\Afield}-\nabla A^0,\qquad
\Bfield=\nabla\times\Afield.
\]
Spatial boldface components are Euclidean components; when a spatial Lorentz index is raised or lowered the mostly-minus metric supplies the corresponding sign.

